# Final production build: what it is

`app.py` = your `app (66)` (Upstox, Yahoo chart loader, AI Backtest Trainer) merged with all earlier fixes,
plus production hardening. `institutional_upgrades.py` = the corrected module (replaces `institutional_upgrades (4)`).

## Setup
1. `pip install -r requirements.txt`
2. Secrets / environment (never put these in code):
   - `ADMIN_PASSWORD`  : your admin password. If unset, a random one-time password is shown on the login screen on first run.
   - `ELITE_DATA_DIR`  : path of a PERSISTENT folder/volume. Without it, Streamlit Cloud erases the journal and paper account on restart.
3. `streamlit run app.py`
4. Upstox: Settings -> enter API key, secret, redirect URI -> open the login link -> paste the returned code. Tokens expire daily; the app now tells you and falls back to Yahoo (clearly labelled).

## Production hardening added in this round
- Passwords: salted PBKDF2 (240k iterations). Old SHA-256 hashes still log in and are upgraded automatically. No more default admin123; the sidebar warns if the old default is still active. Slow-down after 5 failed logins.
- Backups: at most one per file per 10 minutes (previously one per write, which erased real history within minutes).
- Error log capped at 500 rows. Data folder configurable. Upstox 401 -> token cleared + visible "reconnect" message (no silent empty data).

